  "$Comment": "Tomas the Miller's look, every piece of it the game's own: the player's body and a square face with a moustache, short hair under a floppy cap dyed white, as if the flour got to it, the character creator's peasant shirt under a farmer's vest, baggy work trousers and heavy work boots. Parent Seasons_Of_Orbis_Villager brings the player's body, its animations and its hitbox, as Parent Player does for the temple's own Mithril Guard, and the wave he greets a player with. The body, face, mouth and ears share one skin tone (GradientSet Skin, GradientId 08): change all four together. DefaultAttachments replaces the parent's list whole, so the face pieces come first. Under a hat the character creator swaps a haircut for its generic one (HaircutFallbacks), so the hair here is GenericShort. A greyscale texture takes its colour from GradientSet and GradientId, the dyes the character creator offers players: change a GradientId to re-dye one piece.",
